  """Pacherenc du Vic-Bilh is the white-wine twin of Madiran, from the same area. Its name in Gascon means 'posts in a row' (*piquets en rang*), from the old way of training vines on stakes. It is made dry or sweet; the sweet versions, from Petit and Gros Manseng shrivelled on the vine (passerillé), can be picked as late as December. The local Arrufiac grape, nearly extinct, was revived by the Plaimont cooperative and Alain Brumont.""",
