  """Saint-Mont, in the Gers, is almost entirely the work of the Plaimont cooperative, founded in 1979 by André Dubosc, whose campaign to save local grapes and old vineyards earned it the AOC in 2011. In Sarragachies, Plaimont protects a pre-phylloxera vineyard of under a hectare with about 20 varieties, some found nowhere else; in 2012 it became the first vineyard in France listed as a Monument Historique. The reds are Tannat blends, less tannic than Madiran; the whites are fresh and floral.""",
