  """Irouléguy is France's only Basque wine appellation, a small vineyard in the Pyrenean foothills near Saint-Jean-Pied-de-Port on the pilgrimage route to Santiago. Monks of the Roncesvalles abbey planted the first vines. Steep slopes are terraced on red sandstone at up to 400 m. Tannat dominates the reds, which are fresher and more mineral than Madiran's. Domaine Arretxea, Domaine Ilarria, Domaine Brana and the cooperative are the main producers.""",
